cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below. A journal article is in preparation."
type: software
title: "ANKYRA: anchoring a time-series foundation model to each unit's own history for month-ahead load forecasting"
abstract: >-
  ANKYRA is a month-ahead hourly load forecaster for buildings, industrial meters and households. For each unit it
  combines the zero-shot forecast of a frozen time-series foundation model (TimesFM 2.5) with a forecast built from
  the unit's own history, using weights set by the unit's errors at its own completed pseudo-forecast origins. No
  network is trained or fine-tuned. An exact decomposition of the 744-hour trajectory into monthly level, daily path
  and within-day shape provides energy, peak and interval readouts. The repository contains the package, its tests
  and exact properties, the scored results against 20 forecasters on ten populations and four external
  populations, and the code that regenerates every figure.
